<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Son Ngoc Thanh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1908–1977</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Son Ngoc Thanh was a Cambodian nationalist who co-founded the Khmer-language newspaper Nagaravatta in 1936 and fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1942. Back in 1945, he became foreign minister and in August prime minister of the Japanese-sponsored Kingdom of Kampuchea, but the returning French arrested him in October. He later led the anti-royalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Serei and was briefly prime minister of the Khmer Republic in 1972.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/son-ngoc-thanh.jpg" alt="Son Ngoc Thanh" width="292" height="339" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sơn Ngọc Thành · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S%C6%A1n_Ng%E1%BB%8Dc_Th%C3%A0nh_in_1936_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
